<h2>About</h2>

<p>
  For a decade I led cross-functional teams at national scale — managing $17M program portfolios,
  designing evaluation systems, and translating between technical and non-technical stakeholders.
  I learned to think in systems: how information flows, where coordination breaks down, and what
  makes complex projects actually ship.
</p>

<p>
  Now I do the same thing with AI.
</p>

<p>
  I build tools that sit at the boundary between humans and AI systems.
  <a href="https://github.com/thrialectics/threadlinking">Threadlinking</a> is a published npm
  package that preserves decision context across AI sessions.
  <a href="https://apo-pitch.netlify.app/">Apo</a> is a constraint-first specification language
  that improved intent recall from 51% to 91% in early testing. Both grew out of the same
  question: how do you make AI collaboration actually work?
</p>

<p>
  I'm looking for a role focused on human-AI interaction — somewhere I can be both strategic
  and hands-on, on a small team building something that matters.
</p>

